# Admin listings: bulk actions and row-action menu

Applies when creating a list page and when touching one that lacks these.

## Selection and bulk actions (frontend)

- A checkbox per row, plus **Select all** (current filtered rows) and **Cancel**. Keep the selection across filtering; drop deleted ids.
- The bulk bar appears only when something is selected and shows the count.
- **Bulk delete** is always offered (confirmed first). Add **type-specific bulk actions** wherever the model has a status-like field: approve/unapprove, publish/draft, active/inactive. Non-destructive actions need no confirm.
- Update affected rows in place instead of refetching; disable bulk buttons while a request runs.
- Export respects the selection when something is selected. New labels go in every UI language file.

## Bulk endpoints (backend)

- `POST /<version>/<things>/bulk-delete` and `POST /<version>/<things>/bulk-<action>`, registered **before** `apiResource`, with their own throttle limiter (`laravel/rate-limits.mdc`).
- Payload `{ ids: int[] (min 1, max 500, exists), …action fields }` validated by a Form Request.
- Authorize with `bulkDelete` / `bulkUpdate` abilities (`laravel/requests-and-policies.mdc`).
- One `whereIn(...)->update()` / `->delete()`; return `{ updated|deleted: count, message }`.
- Feature test for success, validation failure, and forbidden.

## Row actions

- Every per-row action (edit, open builder, view, duplicate, export, set default, delete) goes in the shared row-actions dropdown component (e.g. `AdminRowActionsMenu`), not inline buttons. Extend that component; never copy its markup.
- The trigger's label names the row (`Actions: <row title>`) for screen readers; items are links or `<button type="button">` with `role="menuitem"`.
- Order: edit → builder → view (`target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"`) → secondary actions → separator → destructive (danger style, confirmed).
- Hide actions the row can't take instead of showing dead items.
- Actions column header is right-aligned (`text-end`); on card grids the menu sits in the card's top-end corner.
- The menu is `position: fixed` so scrolling tables don't clip it and it opens upward near the viewport bottom; don't add `overflow-visible` hacks.
- Stay inline: selection checkboxes, the bulk bar, cell-value controls (a role select, an approve toggle), and header actions (Create, Import, Export all).
